From 059b392b24bbbbcdf45752331b5a68cc3555336b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Bulakh <him@necauq.ua>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:10:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] layout~: add ignore-offscreen-windows-input option

GTK and Electron windows have an input region past their geometry for
the shadows and resize borders of client-side decorations. When such a
window is just off screen, this region extends onto the screen, and the
pointer at the screen edge focuses the hidden window with
focus-follows-mouse.

With the new flag, pointer input skips tiles that are fully outside of
the view. The overview keeps input for all tiles.

See https://github.com/niri-wm/niri/issues/4621
---
