 niri-config/src/layout.rs          |  5 +++++
 niri-config/src/lib.rs             |  1 +
 src/layout/monitor.rs              |  4 ++--
 src/layout/scrolling.rs            | 10 +++++++++-
 src/layout/tile.rs                 | 10 ++++++++++
 src/layout/workspace.rs            | 13 ++++++++++---
 7 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Layout.md b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Layout.md
index 5e5e2a5..1b12a26 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Layout.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Layout.md
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ layout {
     center-focused-column "never"
     always-center-single-column
     empty-workspace-above-first
+    ignore-offscreen-windows-input
     default-column-display "tabbed"
     background-color "#003300"
 
@@ -154,6 +155,24 @@ layout {
 }
 ```
 
+### `ignore-offscreen-windows-input`
+
+If set, windows that are fully outside of the view do not get pointer input.
+
+The input region of some windows extends past their visible area, for example for the shadows and the resize borders of client-side decorations (GTK and Electron apps do this).
+When such a window is just off screen, this invisible area can extend onto the screen.
+Then the pointer at the edge of the screen goes to the hidden window: [focus-follows-mouse](./Configuration:-Input.md#focus-follows-mouse) focuses it and scrolls the view to it, and a click starts to resize it.
+
+With this flag, the pointer goes through such windows.
+Windows that are partially on screen keep their full input region.
+In the overview, all windows get input as usual.
+
+```kdl
+layout {
+    ignore-offscreen-windows-input
+}
+```
+
 ### `default-column-display`
 
 <sup>Since: 25.02</sup>
